Awesome-Science-Agents licensing scope

This repository contains software, collection content, and third-party material.
The following policy takes effect when this licensing change is merged into main.

Software: MIT for new contributions
----------------------------------
New original software contributions submitted under this policy are licensed
under the MIT License in LICENSES/MIT.txt. This covers the website template
(HTML, CSS, and JavaScript), build scripts, tests, and software configuration.
The copyright notice identifies the respective contributors; listing someone
as a maintainer does not transfer ownership of their work.

Existing CC0 material
--------------------
The CC0 dedication already applied to repository-owned material through commit
4fae6231ae2d886aaf4432227b807d0109fe07e8 remains effective. The original license
text is preserved unchanged in LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt. Any other material validly
released under CC0 before this policy took effect also retains that status.
This policy does not revoke those permissions or impose MIT conditions on
previously CC0-covered portions, including when carried forward into later
versions or downloaded after this change. New copyrightable software additions
submitted under this policy are covered by MIT; the earlier portions remain
available under CC0.

Collection content: CC0 1.0 Universal
------------------------------------
Original paper-list entries, reading guides, documentation, and catalog data
continue to use CC0 1.0 Universal, unless a specific notice states otherwise.

Third-party material
--------------------
Referenced papers, external code and platforms, paper figures, and other
third-party material remain subject to their respective rights and licenses.
Neither MIT nor CC0 here grants rights to those materials. Preserve applicable
third-party notices; see docs/assets/paper-figures/README.md for figure sources.

Acknowledgement
---------------
The README includes an optional acknowledgement request and example. Public
credit or a backlink is appreciated but is not an additional license condition.
For MIT-covered software, the MIT copyright and permission notices must still
be retained as required by that license.
